  "id": "irritable-bowel-syndrome",
  "term": "irritable bowel syndrome",
  "definition": "Irritable bowel syndrome is a common disorder of the brain-gut axis marked by abdominal pain linked to bowel movements and changes in stool frequency or form. It is a heterogeneous condition that can reduce daily functioning and quality of life, and within a biopsychosocial view, both bodily and psychosocial factors may contribute to its onset and persistence.",
